          <!-- BODY -->
          <tr>
            <td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:28px 32px;
                       font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#212121;">

              <p>Hello M&amp;K members and friends,</p>

              <p>
                We're excited to announce a new dedicated mailing list
                for the Mike &amp; Key Fox Hunt program:
                <strong><a href="mailto:FoxHunting@mkarc.groups.io">FoxHunting@mkarc.groups.io</a></strong>
              </p>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                Why Join?
              </h3>

              <p>
                The FoxHunting list is your central hub for:
              </p>

              <ul style="margin:8px 0;padding-left:20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Event announcements</strong> &mdash; get
                  details about upcoming fox hunts, including
                  on-foot ARDF events and regional mobile hunts
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Last-minute updates</strong> &mdash; 
                  weather changes, location adjustments, and
                  day-of logistics
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Results and photos</strong> &mdash;
                  post-hunt summaries, results, and event photos
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Discussion and planning</strong> &mdash;
                  share techniques, ask questions, discuss equipment,
                  and coordinate rides
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Build projects</strong> &mdash; learn about
                  antenna builds, loaner equipment, and DIY projects
                </li>
              </ul>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                Who Can Join?
              </h3>

              <p>
                <strong>Everyone is welcome!</strong> The FoxHunting
                list is open to M&amp;K members, visitors, and anyone
                interested in Amateur Radio Direction Finding. You
                don't need to be a club member to participate in fox
                hunts or join the list.
              </p>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                How to Subscribe
              </h3>

              <p>
                Join the list by visiting:
              </p>

              <p style="text-align:center;margin:20px 0;">
                <a href="https://mkarc.groups.io/g/FoxHunting"
                   style="display:inline-block;background-color:#1a3a5c;
                          color:#ffffff;padding:12px 24px;
                          text-decoration:none;border-radius:4px;
                          font-weight:bold;font-size:16px;">
                  Subscribe to FoxHunting List
                </a>
              </p>

              <p style="font-size:13px;color:#555555;">
                Or send a blank email to 
                <a href="mailto:FoxHunting+subscribe@mkarc.groups.io">FoxHunting+subscribe@mkarc.groups.io</a>
              </p>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                Share the Word
              </h3>

              <p>
                Know someone who might be interested in fox hunting?
                <strong>Please forward this announcement</strong> to
                other hams, radio clubs, or mailing lists that might
                enjoy Amateur Radio Direction Finding activities.
                All are welcome!
              </p>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                Upcoming 2026 Events
              </h3>

              <p>
                We have two hunts planned for the remainder of 2026:
              </p>

              <ul style="margin:8px 0;padding-left:20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Saturday, August 22</strong> &mdash;
                  On-foot hunt at Marymoor Park, Redmond
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Sunday, September 20</strong> <em>(tentative)</em>
                  &mdash; Regional mobile hunt in west Snohomish County
                </li>
              </ul>

              <p>
                Full details and reminders will be sent to the
                FoxHunting list as dates approach.
              </p>

              <p>
                Questions? Contact
                <strong>Tom Sayles, KE4HET</strong> at
                <a href="mailto:TSayles@Soot-n-Smoke.com">TSayles@Soot-n-Smoke.com</a>.
              </p>

              <p>
                More information at
                <a href="https://mikeandkey.org/foxhunt.php"
                   style="color:#1a3a5c;">
                  mikeandkey.org/foxhunt.php
                </a>.
              </p>

              <p>73,<br>Tom Sayles, KE4HET<br>Fox Hunt Program Coordinator</p>

